1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:01,460
Our minds aren't

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,390
ready for superintelligence.

3
00:00:03,430 --> 00:00:04,880
We have godlike AI

4
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:06,590
and Stone Age brains.

5
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:08,120
AI gets more capable

6
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:09,350
every few months.

7
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:11,280
And you can't upgrade a brain.

8
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:12,970
You can feel that tonight.

9
00:00:13,210 --> 00:00:14,420
A headline about AI

10
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:15,660
lands on your screen.

11
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:17,340
Big letters.

12
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:18,380
Bad news.

13
00:00:18,530 --> 00:00:19,770
Your pulse jumps.

14
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:22,330
Your thumb is already moving.

15
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:23,990
You decided none of it.

16
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:25,450
That reflex is older

17
00:00:25,490 --> 00:00:26,620
than our species.

18
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:28,070
So if your brain can't

19
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:30,070
catch up in time, what can?

20
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:31,360
Something can.

21
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:32,280
Because the danger

22
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:33,700
was never the machine.

23
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:34,900
It's the gap.

24
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:36,860
The machine's clock is racing.

25
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:39,990
The brain's clock barely moves.

26
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:41,680
But the brain isn't

27
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:43,010
your only clock.

28
00:00:43,230 --> 00:00:44,850
Two others can be set.

29
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:47,780
The slower takes a whole society.

30
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:50,320
The faster takes a single person.

31
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:53,070
And you are carrying it right now.

32
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,190
To see what it is,

33
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:56,800
go back to that headline.

34
00:00:57,270 --> 00:00:58,700
Why did your pulse jump

35
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:00,220
before you had read a word?

36
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:01,970
Because the alarm in your head

37
00:01:02,010 --> 00:01:03,590
is older than reading.

38
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:05,010
Every mammal carries

39
00:01:05,050 --> 00:01:06,060
a version of it.

40
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:07,290
That is the first

41
00:01:07,330 --> 00:01:09,220
of three old reflexes.

42
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,200
Fear, before thought.

43
00:01:11,370 --> 00:01:13,060
And bad news pulls.

44
00:01:13,230 --> 00:01:15,220
In a huge test of news headlines,

45
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:16,550
every extra negative

46
00:01:16,590 --> 00:01:18,300
word brought more clicks.

47
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:19,460
The second reflex

48
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:20,750
feels much better.

49
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:21,900
Somebody near you

50
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:23,330
is getting ahead with AI.

51
00:01:23,370 --> 00:01:24,430
A colleague.

52
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:25,480
A competitor.

53
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:27,170
And something in you says:

54
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:28,960
grab it, before they do.

55
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:30,970
Companies have it too.

56
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:34,130
The biggest pour fortunes into AI,

57
00:01:34,170 --> 00:01:35,890
and say they have no choice.

58
00:01:36,270 --> 00:01:37,840
The scientist who co-chairs

59
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:38,900
the United Nations'

60
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:40,850
panel on AI answered them

61
00:01:40,890 --> 00:01:42,370
at the Security Council:

62
00:01:42,770 --> 00:01:44,560
Citizens and governments

63
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:46,650
should not accept the companies'

64
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:47,500
claim that they are

65
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:49,440
trapped in a race.

66
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:52,080
The race is not a law of nature.

67
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,290
It is the product of choices.

68
00:01:54,810 --> 00:01:56,450
Not a law of nature.

69
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:57,710
A choice.

70
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:01,160
The third reflex is the quiet one,

71
00:02:01,230 --> 00:02:02,740
and it makes us late.

72
00:02:03,110 --> 00:02:04,770
Your brain expects tomorrow

73
00:02:04,810 --> 00:02:07,340
to look like today, plus a little.

74
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:09,480
But this machine doesn't add.

75
00:02:09,590 --> 00:02:10,730
It doubles.

76
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,470
On one leading measure,

77
00:02:12,510 --> 00:02:13,890
the length of a task AI

78
00:02:13,930 --> 00:02:15,340
can finish on its own

79
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:18,250
doubles roughly every 3.5 months.

80
00:02:18,550 --> 00:02:20,370
Even the experts missed.

81
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:22,410
AI reached gold-medal level

82
00:02:22,450 --> 00:02:23,730
at the Math Olympiad

83
00:02:23,770 --> 00:02:25,990
5 years before they expected it.

84
00:02:26,350 --> 00:02:27,730
If even the experts were

85
00:02:27,770 --> 00:02:30,210
that far off on today's machines,

86
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:31,460
whose gut is ready

87
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:33,080
for superintelligence?

88
00:02:33,690 --> 00:02:36,190
To be fair: what defines us,

89
00:02:36,230 --> 00:02:37,960
one researcher wrote this year,

90
00:02:38,150 --> 00:02:39,880
is how well we adapt.

91
00:02:40,230 --> 00:02:41,030
True.

92
00:02:41,070 --> 00:02:43,070
But we adapt over years.

93
00:02:43,210 --> 00:02:45,190
The machine moves in months.

94
00:02:45,510 --> 00:02:47,150
The scientist E. O. Wilson

95
00:02:47,190 --> 00:02:48,590
had a sentence for this,

96
00:02:48,630 --> 00:02:50,470
long before ChatGPT:

97
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:54,210
…modern humanity is distinguished

98
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:56,900
by Paleolithic emotions

99
00:02:56,940 --> 00:03:00,440
and medieval institutions

100
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:03,790
like banks and religions

101
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:07,050
and godlike technology.

102
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:09,710
He wasn't talking about AI.

103
00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:11,140
But listen to the middle

104
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:12,270
of his sentence.

105
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:13,750
Institutions.

106
00:03:13,790 --> 00:03:14,630
Rules.

107
00:03:14,670 --> 00:03:15,670
Laws.

108
00:03:15,770 --> 00:03:17,440
A seat belt for the brain:

109
00:03:17,650 --> 00:03:19,040
it holds, even when

110
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,650
you aren't paying attention.

111
00:03:20,870 --> 00:03:23,350
So how fast do rules move?

112
00:03:24,510 --> 00:03:26,200
Take Europe's AI law.

113
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:26,930
It was proposed

114
00:03:26,970 --> 00:03:29,070
before ChatGPT existed.

115
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:29,910
Its last rules

116
00:03:29,950 --> 00:03:31,910
won't apply until 2028.

117
00:03:31,970 --> 00:03:33,570
More than 7 years.

118
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:34,880
For a machine that doubles

119
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:36,030
every few months.

120
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:37,660
Not out of laziness:

121
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:39,060
those rules were pushed back

122
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:40,310
because the standards needed

123
00:03:40,350 --> 00:03:41,940
to apply them weren't ready.

124
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:43,440
So are rules just

125
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:44,730
too slow for this?

126
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:46,330
One case says no.

127
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:48,680
In the 1980s, scientists reported

128
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,400
a hole in the ozone layer.

129
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,180
A little over 2 years later,

130
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:53,570
a treaty was signed.

131
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:55,730
And that treaty has

132
00:03:55,770 --> 00:03:57,220
an update built in.

133
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:58,300
It can be tightened

134
00:03:58,340 --> 00:03:59,800
without starting over.

135
00:04:00,020 --> 00:04:02,260
It has been, again and again.

136
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:04,000
The sky still needs

137
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:05,330
decades to heal.

138
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,290
But the rule came fast,

139
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:08,510
and it kept learning.

140
00:04:08,730 --> 00:04:11,080
So the slower clock can be set.

141
00:04:11,270 --> 00:04:12,320
It has been done.

142
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:14,310
Just not in a few months.

143
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:16,470
This channel exists

144
00:04:16,510 --> 00:04:17,820
for one reason:

145
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:18,830
so that the arrival

146
00:04:18,870 --> 00:04:20,010
of superintelligence

147
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:21,820
goes well for everybody.

148
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:23,560
Stone Age brains and all.

149
00:04:23,830 --> 00:04:24,830
Want that too?

150
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:25,980
Then subscribe.

151
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:28,580
Is there anything that moves

152
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:29,930
faster than a law?

153
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:31,280
There is.

154
00:04:31,330 --> 00:04:32,300
And it isn't

155
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:33,760
out-thinking the machine.

156
00:04:33,990 --> 00:04:36,130
You won't, and you don't have to.

157
00:04:36,530 --> 00:04:38,240
It's the clock you are carrying:

158
00:04:38,470 --> 00:04:40,020
how fast you notice what

159
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:41,640
is happening inside you.

160
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:44,720
Yuval Noah Harari writes about AI,

161
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:46,280
and has books to sell.

162
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:47,590
He has a bigger word

163
00:04:47,630 --> 00:04:48,630
for that clock.

164
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:49,810
And a price.

165
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,530
…if for every $10

166
00:04:51,570 --> 00:04:52,900
we spend on developing

167
00:04:52,940 --> 00:04:54,520
artificial intelligence,

168
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:57,440
we could invest at least $1

169
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,680
in developing our consciousness,

170
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:01,790
I think we'll be okay.

171
00:05:01,830 --> 00:05:06,080
But this is not the current

172
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,740
trajectory we are on.

173
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:10,330
Developing our consciousness.

174
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:12,180
What is that supposed to mean?

175
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,730
A retreat on a mountain?

176
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:15,620
He means something plainer:

177
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,130
knowing your own mind

178
00:05:17,170 --> 00:05:18,630
well enough to notice what

179
00:05:18,670 --> 00:05:20,460
a machine is doing to it.

180
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:21,860
Try something.

181
00:05:22,010 --> 00:05:23,660
Start a sentence in your head,

182
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:24,370
and watch where

183
00:05:24,410 --> 00:05:25,650
the words come from.

184
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:26,880
You can't tell.

185
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,040
Harari says he can't, either.

186
00:05:29,190 --> 00:05:30,750
So much of your own mind

187
00:05:30,790 --> 00:05:32,230
runs unwatched.

188
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:34,020
Developing consciousness means

189
00:05:34,060 --> 00:05:35,450
watching more of it.

190
00:05:35,650 --> 00:05:36,890
Not getting smarter.

191
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:38,140
Noticing.

192
00:05:38,470 --> 00:05:39,860
This is fear.

193
00:05:40,150 --> 00:05:41,630
This is craving.

194
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,890
This is something pulling at you.

195
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:45,440
Why now?

196
00:05:45,570 --> 00:05:46,160
Because you have

197
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,840
competition, he says.

198
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:49,400
Companies and governments

199
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:50,420
are working to know you

200
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:52,200
better than you know yourself.

201
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:53,620
And whoever does

202
00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:55,120
can sell you anything.

203
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:57,360
A product, or a politician.

204
00:05:57,590 --> 00:06:00,070
The idea: a reflex you notice

205
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:02,020
is harder to use against you.

206
00:06:02,310 --> 00:06:04,590
So is meditation the answer?

207
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:05,780
It's his.

208
00:06:05,910 --> 00:06:07,030
On his first course,

209
00:06:07,070 --> 00:06:08,570
he was told to do nothing

210
00:06:08,610 --> 00:06:10,060
but notice his breath.

211
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:11,120
He couldn't manage

212
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:12,780
more than 10 seconds.

213
00:06:13,330 --> 00:06:14,940
Whether that is your way

214
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:16,010
stays open.

215
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:17,430
The smallest version

216
00:06:17,470 --> 00:06:18,780
takes one breath,

217
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:19,710
between the headline

218
00:06:19,750 --> 00:06:20,750
and your thumb.

219
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:23,190
It hands the decision back to you,

220
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,390
before a headline tuned

221
00:06:24,430 --> 00:06:25,930
for clicks takes it.

222
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:27,910
But one person noticing

223
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:29,440
is the small version.

224
00:06:29,710 --> 00:06:31,040
Harari's dollar is meant

225
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:32,180
for the big one:

226
00:06:32,370 --> 00:06:34,320
understanding the mind itself.

227
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:36,530
And look where the money goes.

228
00:06:36,690 --> 00:06:38,530
This year, four tech giants

229
00:06:38,570 --> 00:06:39,270
plan to spend

230
00:06:39,310 --> 00:06:41,930
more than $700 billion,

231
00:06:41,970 --> 00:06:43,410
mostly on AI.

232
00:06:43,660 --> 00:06:44,710
America's flagship

233
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:46,100
brain research program

234
00:06:46,140 --> 00:06:48,260
got about 430 million

235
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:49,630
in its last budget.

236
00:06:50,190 --> 00:06:52,280
Those pots aren't the same thing,

237
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:54,300
and his ratio is a wish,

238
00:06:54,340 --> 00:06:55,700
not a calculation.

239
00:06:56,010 --> 00:06:56,780
But they show where

240
00:06:56,820 --> 00:06:58,100
the attention is.

241
00:06:58,360 --> 00:07:00,050
And what we don't understand,

242
00:07:00,090 --> 00:07:01,200
we don't measure.

243
00:07:01,710 --> 00:07:04,590
AI gets graded on how smart it is.

244
00:07:04,890 --> 00:07:07,150
Harari asks a different question:

245
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,180
what does it do

246
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:09,900
to the person using it?

247
00:07:10,290 --> 00:07:12,180
One early test exists.

248
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:14,270
A small group of researchers put

249
00:07:14,310 --> 00:07:17,070
everyday questions to 15 chatbots.

250
00:07:17,310 --> 00:07:19,270
Nearly all failed to respect

251
00:07:19,310 --> 00:07:20,570
the user's attention.

252
00:07:20,830 --> 00:07:21,700
Told to ignore

253
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:23,110
the user's wellbeing,

254
00:07:23,150 --> 00:07:25,640
about two thirds turned harmful.

255
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:28,490
So that is what the dollar is for.

256
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:29,880
Noticing yourself.

257
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:31,540
Studying the mind.

258
00:07:31,620 --> 00:07:32,830
And grading the machine

259
00:07:32,870 --> 00:07:34,470
on what it does to us.

260
00:07:34,750 --> 00:07:36,180
But one calm person

261
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:37,870
doesn't slow a race.

262
00:07:38,170 --> 00:07:39,590
What if you get faster,

263
00:07:39,630 --> 00:07:41,030
and the rules don't?

264
00:07:42,210 --> 00:07:43,740
Then you notice more,

265
00:07:43,870 --> 00:07:45,320
and the race runs on.

266
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:47,060
So set both clocks,

267
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,210
and picture an evening

268
00:07:48,250 --> 00:07:49,690
a few years from now.

269
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:51,660
The headline still arrives.

270
00:07:51,700 --> 00:07:53,560
Your pulse still jumps.

271
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,640
But in this version,

272
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:55,770
the app in your hand

273
00:07:55,810 --> 00:07:57,140
carries a grade.

274
00:07:57,340 --> 00:07:58,910
Not for how clever it is.

275
00:07:59,090 --> 00:07:59,790
For what it does

276
00:07:59,830 --> 00:08:01,420
to the people who use it.

277
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:03,360
It was tested before release,

278
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,150
and again every few months.

279
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:06,560
When something goes wrong,

280
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,590
the rule changes within the year.

281
00:08:08,710 --> 00:08:09,180
And you know

282
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:10,950
your reflexes by name.

283
00:08:11,230 --> 00:08:12,230
Far away?

284
00:08:12,270 --> 00:08:13,620
Take that evening apart.

285
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:14,740
The grade?

286
00:08:14,780 --> 00:08:16,680
You just heard an early test.

287
00:08:17,270 --> 00:08:18,890
Testing before release?

288
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,400
Demis Hassabis,

289
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:22,540
a co-founder of Google DeepMind,

290
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:24,370
has proposed a body that tests

291
00:08:24,410 --> 00:08:25,900
the most powerful models

292
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:27,100
before launch.

293
00:08:27,390 --> 00:08:28,900
The tests would be renewed,

294
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:30,350
perhaps every quarter.

295
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:32,890
Rules that move within a year?

296
00:08:33,270 --> 00:08:34,030
Last month,

297
00:08:34,070 --> 00:08:35,640
the head of the United Nations

298
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:37,290
called for a global framework

299
00:08:37,330 --> 00:08:39,540
for AI risks, within one year.

300
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:41,550
And the pressure is there.

301
00:08:41,900 --> 00:08:42,360
According to

302
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:44,190
the UN's technology envoy,

303
00:08:44,230 --> 00:08:46,550
in 2017 three world leaders

304
00:08:46,590 --> 00:08:48,230
raised concerns about AI

305
00:08:48,270 --> 00:08:50,120
at the UN General Assembly.

306
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:53,210
This year, 135 did.

307
00:08:53,770 --> 00:08:55,290
None of it is settled.

308
00:08:55,550 --> 00:08:57,640
The framework is not a treaty.

309
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:59,250
The testing body would be paid

310
00:08:59,290 --> 00:09:01,630
mostly by the industry it tests.

311
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,010
And it is not the course we're on.

312
00:09:04,150 --> 00:09:05,790
Harari says so himself.

313
00:09:06,470 --> 00:09:07,150
But the race

314
00:09:07,190 --> 00:09:09,060
is a product of choices.

315
00:09:09,190 --> 00:09:10,380
So is the gap.

316
00:09:10,690 --> 00:09:12,950
Labs can test before they ship.

317
00:09:13,270 --> 00:09:14,630
Governments can write rules

318
00:09:14,670 --> 00:09:16,250
with the update built in.

319
00:09:16,490 --> 00:09:18,350
Voters can demand both.

320
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:19,720
And one clock needs

321
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:21,040
no vote at all.

322
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,040
Tonight, or tomorrow,

323
00:09:24,150 --> 00:09:24,960
the next headline

324
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,290
lands on your screen.

325
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:27,820
Same big letters.

326
00:09:27,870 --> 00:09:28,910
Same pulse.

327
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:31,660
The reflex hasn't changed,

328
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:32,700
and it won't.

329
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:34,880
But this time, you notice it.

330
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:36,590
This is fear.

331
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:38,180
You take one breath.

332
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,420
And then you decide

333
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:41,680
what your thumb does.

334
00:09:41,990 --> 00:09:43,340
That is the first clock

335
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:44,370
you can set.

336
00:09:44,410 --> 00:09:45,800
It took a single breath.

337
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:48,130
The other one takes all of us:

338
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:49,730
rules that learn as fast

339
00:09:49,770 --> 00:09:51,020
as the machine does.

340
00:09:51,270 --> 00:09:53,180
The gap won't close completely.

341
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,390
It can get small enough

342
00:09:54,430 --> 00:09:55,630
that we still steer.

343
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:57,640
We can't upgrade our brains.

344
00:09:57,770 --> 00:09:59,680
We can upgrade our minds,

345
00:09:59,770 --> 00:10:01,150
and our rules.

346
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:03,500
This channel exists

347
00:10:03,540 --> 00:10:04,430
so that the arrival

348
00:10:04,470 --> 00:10:05,610
of superintelligence

349
00:10:05,650 --> 00:10:07,370
goes well for everybody.

350
00:10:07,590 --> 00:10:09,240
That takes minds that notice,

351
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:10,840
and rules that keep up.

352
00:10:11,070 --> 00:10:12,070
Want that too?

353
00:10:12,110 --> 00:10:13,110
Then subscribe.

